<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, oil subdued, meal up.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, oil subdued, meal up.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices fell by 500-600 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on Monday on improved arrivals, traders said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices also fell sharply on heavy selling by processing plants. Soyoil solvent was down by 500 rupees per tonne and soyoil refined by 300 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices improved on limited supply. Soymeal yellow was quoted at $262-263 per tonne in export deals. Rapeseed extraction was offered at $127-128 per tonne for export. It was quoted at 4,300 rupees FOR Bedibunder and at 4,250-4,275 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
